From 024e19bf49f9981f8e9039242736045434a5e638 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Seyoon Ragavan <complexzetaprime@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:11:36 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Abstract register machines: per-instruction step equations
 and block embedding

Adds the value semantics of each instruction as an equation (Machines/ARM), a congruence for a
call's virtual input (Machines/Program), and the embedding of a machine as a block of a larger
one: Ins.embed, RegExt, preS_of_ins, preS_embed, astep_embed and AHalt.embed
(Machines/ARMProof), with the bounded-guard form AHalt.embed_guardLe (Machines/ARMLoops).
The Savitch machine is shown to have no input-format check (SavitchARM.A_noVal), so its proved
runs transport into a host machine unchanged. Additive only: no existing statement changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
